		<item>
		<title>Bronson Reed confirmed to be back home after hospital stay in Saudi Arabia following WWE Crown Jewel</title>
		<link>https://www.wrestleview.com/featured-top-story/397861-bronson-reed-confirmed-to-be-back-home-after-hospital-stay-in-saudi-arabia-following-wwe-crown-jewel/</link>
					<comments>https://www.wrestleview.com/featured-top-story/397861-bronson-reed-confirmed-to-be-back-home-after-hospital-stay-in-saudi-arabia-following-wwe-crown-jewel/#respond</comments>
		
		<dc:creator><![CDATA[Jerome Wilen]]></dc:creator>
		<pubDate>Wed, 18 Nov 2026 20:14:54 +0000</pubDate>
				<category><![CDATA[Featured Top Story]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[WWE News]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[Bronson Reed]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[Crown Jewel]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[home]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[hospital]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[WWE]]></category>
		<guid isPermaLink="false">https://www.wrestleview.com/?p=397861</guid>

					<description><![CDATA[<p>As first reported by F4WOnline, then confirmed by Fightful, WWE&#8217;s Bronson Reed is back home after suffering umultiple&#8230;</p>
<p>The post <a href="https://www.wrestleview.com/featured-top-story/397861-bronson-reed-confirmed-to-be-back-home-after-hospital-stay-in-saudi-arabia-following-wwe-crown-jewel/">Bronson Reed confirmed to be back home after hospital stay in Saudi Arabia following WWE Crown Jewel</a> appeared first on <a href="https://www.wrestleview.com">WWE News, WWE Results, AEW News, AEW Results</a>.</p>
]]></description>
										<content:encoded><![CDATA[
<p class="wp-block-paragraph">As first reported by <a href="https://www.f4wonline.com/news/wwe/bronson-reed-back-home-after-suffering-injuries-at-wwe-crown-jewel-exclusive/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener">F4WOnline</a>, then confirmed by Fightful, WWE&#8217;s Bronson Reed is back home after suffering umultiple broken ribs and a lacerated kidney, due to a spot at Crown Jewel where Oba Femi slammed him through a table off the stage area.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Reed was hospitalized in Saudi Arabia following the injury, being treated for his injuries. WWE had assigned medical personnel to stay with Reed and had their top international executive onsite to ensure Reed had been given VIP treatment.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">There is still no timeline of when Reed will return to in-ring action. </p>



<figure class="wp-block-image size-full"><img fetchpriority="high" decoding="async" width="697" height="310" src="https://www.wrestleview.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/image-7.png" alt="" class="wp-image-397862" srcset="https://www.wrestleview.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/image-7.png 697w, https://www.wrestleview.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/image-7-600x267.png 600w, https://www.wrestleview.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/image-7-380x169.png 380w, https://www.wrestleview.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/image-7-550x244.png 550w" sizes="(max-width: 697px) 100vw, 697px" /></figure>



<figure class="wp-block-embed is-type-video is-provider-youtube wp-block-embed-youtube wp-embed-aspect-16-9 wp-has-aspect-ratio"><div class="wp-block-embed__wrapper">
<iframe title="Bronson Reed Still Hospitalized After Crown Jewel 2026: What Really Happened" width="1200" height="675" src="https://www.youtube.com/embed/bZIy5c8hXjY?feature=oembed" frameborder="0" allow="accelerometer; autoplay; clipboard-write; encrypted-media; gyroscope; picture-in-picture; web-share" referrerpolicy="strict-origin-when-cross-origin" allowfullscreen></iframe>
</div></figure>
<p>The post <a href="https://www.wrestleview.com/featured-top-story/397861-bronson-reed-confirmed-to-be-back-home-after-hospital-stay-in-saudi-arabia-following-wwe-crown-jewel/">Bronson Reed confirmed to be back home after hospital stay in Saudi Arabia following WWE Crown Jewel</a> appeared first on <a href="https://www.wrestleview.com">WWE News, WWE Results, AEW News, AEW Results</a>.</p>
]]></content:encoded>
					
					<wfw:commentRss>https://www.wrestleview.com/featured-top-story/397861-bronson-reed-confirmed-to-be-back-home-after-hospital-stay-in-saudi-arabia-following-wwe-crown-jewel/feed/</wfw:commentRss>
			<slash:comments>0</slash:comments>
		
		
			</item>
		<item>
		<title>Potential location revealed for next year&#8217;s AEW All In pay-per-view</title>
		<link>https://www.wrestleview.com/aew-news/397857-potential-location-revealed-for-next-years-aew-all-in-pay-per-view/</link>
					<comments>https://www.wrestleview.com/aew-news/397857-potential-location-revealed-for-next-years-aew-all-in-pay-per-view/#respond</comments>
		
		<dc:creator><![CDATA[Jerome Wilen]]></dc:creator>
		<pubDate>Wed, 18 Nov 2026 20:03:49 +0000</pubDate>
				<category><![CDATA[AEW News]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[AEW]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[All In]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[Toronto]]></category>
		<guid isPermaLink="false">https://www.wrestleview.com/?p=397857</guid>

					<description><![CDATA[<p>Fightful Select is reporting that Toronto, Ontario, Canada is being discussed internally within AEW as a potential location&#8230;</p>
<p>The post <a href="https://www.wrestleview.com/aew-news/397857-potential-location-revealed-for-next-years-aew-all-in-pay-per-view/">Potential location revealed for next year&#8217;s AEW All In pay-per-view</a> appeared first on <a href="https://www.wrestleview.com">WWE News, WWE Results, AEW News, AEW Results</a>.</p>
]]></description>
										<content:encoded><![CDATA[
<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Fightful Select is reporting that Toronto, Ontario, Canada is <a href="https://www.fightful.com/wrestling/toronto-discussed-as-potential-landing-spot-for-aew-all-in-2027/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">being discussed internally within AEW</a> as a potential location for next year&#8217;s All In pay-per-view. </p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">The report notes that if Toronto was to be the location, the event would likely featured Adam Copeland&#8217;s retirement match. Copeland announced during the October 14 three-hour Dynamite/Collision on TBS. It should be noted that All In has traditionally taken place in July or the end of August. </p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"></p>
<p>The post <a href="https://www.wrestleview.com/aew-news/397857-potential-location-revealed-for-next-years-aew-all-in-pay-per-view/">Potential location revealed for next year&#8217;s AEW All In pay-per-view</a> appeared first on <a href="https://www.wrestleview.com">WWE News, WWE Results, AEW News, AEW Results</a>.</p>
]]></content:encoded>
					
					<wfw:commentRss>https://www.wrestleview.com/aew-news/397857-potential-location-revealed-for-next-years-aew-all-in-pay-per-view/feed/</wfw:commentRss>
			<slash:comments>0</slash:comments>
		
		
			</item>
		<item>
		<title>The Rock announces appearance for Survivor Series: WarGames</title>
		<link>https://www.wrestleview.com/featured-top-story/397849-the-rock-announces-appearance-for-survivor-series-wargames/</link>
					<comments>https://www.wrestleview.com/featured-top-story/397849-the-rock-announces-appearance-for-survivor-series-wargames/#respond</comments>
		
		<dc:creator><![CDATA[Jerome Wilen]]></dc:creator>
		<pubDate>Wed, 18 Nov 2026 19:56:44 +0000</pubDate>
				<category><![CDATA[Featured Top Story]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[WWE News]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[Dwayne Johnson]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[Houston]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[Survivor Series]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[The Rock]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[WWE]]></category>
		<guid isPermaLink="false">https://www.wrestleview.com/?p=397849</guid>

					<description><![CDATA[<p>During his appearance on Wednesday&#8217;s episode of The Pat McAfee Show, Dwayne “The Rock” Johnson announced he will&#8230;</p>
<p>The post <a href="https://www.wrestleview.com/featured-top-story/397849-the-rock-announces-appearance-for-survivor-series-wargames/">The Rock announces appearance for Survivor Series: WarGames</a> appeared first on <a href="https://www.wrestleview.com">WWE News, WWE Results, AEW News, AEW Results</a>.</p>
]]></description>
										<content:encoded><![CDATA[
<p class="wp-block-paragraph">During his appearance on Wednesday&#8217;s episode of The Pat McAfee Show, Dwayne “The Rock” Johnson announced he will be at Survivor Series: WarGames, which will emanate from Daikin Park in Houston, Texas on Saturday, November 28 beginning at 6:00 pm ET/3:00 pm PT.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Johnson, under the name Rocky Miavia, made his official debut with WWE/F at Survivor Series on November 17, 1996, which was held at Madison Square Garden in New York City. </p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><em>“Here’s the truth is, I would not miss next week for the world, man. So I’m going to Houston. Houston, we don’t have a problem. I’m going to Houston, and I’m going to go to Survivor Series…People’s Champ is coming home. I’ll see everybody next week at Survivor Series.”</em></p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Johnson also revealed to McAfee, that he will be the celebrity guest picker for this Saturday&#8217;s ESPN College GameDay at the University of Miami (Hurricanes), where Johnson played football. He was a member of the 1991 team that won a national championship. He played in 39 games with one start and recorded 4.5 sacks and 77 tackles.</p>



<figure class="wp-block-embed is-type-rich is-provider-x wp-block-embed-x"><div class="wp-block-embed__wrapper">
<blockquote class="twitter-tweet" data-width="550" data-dnt="true"><p lang="en" dir="ltr">We appreciate you <a href="https://x.com/TheRock?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw">@TheRock</a> <a href="https://x.com/hashtag/PMSLive?src=hash&amp;ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw">#PMSLive</a> <a href="https://t.co/ADRXaeePs4">pic.twitter.com/ADRXaeePs4</a></p>&mdash; Pat McAfee (@PatMcAfeeShow) <a href="https://x.com/PatMcAfeeShow/status/2123112334633959604?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw">November 18, 2026</a></blockquote><script async src="https://platform.x.com/widgets.js" charset="utf-8"></script>
</div></figure>



<figure class="wp-block-embed is-type-video is-provider-youtube wp-block-embed-youtube wp-embed-aspect-16-9 wp-has-aspect-ratio"><div class="wp-block-embed__wrapper">
<iframe title="The Rock makes his WWE debut: WWE Survivor Series 1996" width="1200" height="675" src="https://www.youtube.com/embed/vsei2mtBzVA?feature=oembed" frameborder="0" allow="accelerometer; autoplay; clipboard-write; encrypted-media; gyroscope; picture-in-picture; web-share" referrerpolicy="strict-origin-when-cross-origin" allowfullscreen></iframe>
</div></figure>
<p>The post <a href="https://www.wrestleview.com/featured-top-story/397849-the-rock-announces-appearance-for-survivor-series-wargames/">The Rock announces appearance for Survivor Series: WarGames</a> appeared first on <a href="https://www.wrestleview.com">WWE News, WWE Results, AEW News, AEW Results</a>.</p>
]]></content:encoded>
					
					<wfw:commentRss>https://www.wrestleview.com/featured-top-story/397849-the-rock-announces-appearance-for-survivor-series-wargames/feed/</wfw:commentRss>
			<slash:comments>0</slash:comments>
		
		
			</item>
